From 400ae07fa9ea6f4fe3e15a174fe5682bfe826911 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Radiarch Project <radiarch@invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:15:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] GPU transport prototype: protons, electromagnetic physics,
 full dose (MCSQUARE_GPU=1)

Simulation_loop hands over to gpu_Simulation_loop when MCSQUARE_GPU=1. MCsquare's own Generate_PBS_particle samples
the primaries on the CPU in batches; gpu_transport.cu transports them on a CUDA device, one history per thread
(as FRED and Wan Chan Tseung 2015 describe), following hadron_step for a proton step by step: VoxelInterface
stepping, PSTAR/Geant4 stopping powers, restricted energy loss (Compute_dE2), straggling, Fippel multiple
scattering, hard ionization with local deposit. Philox random numbers; float atomics per batch, folded into double.
Nuclear interactions, LET, prompt gammas, energy scoring, independent grids and beamlet mode are not supported and
stop the run. Materials record the length of their stopping-power table (Nbr_SP) for the copy to the device.
